    "media:imagetext": "Amb\n062717A\nSanibel, F orida\nJuly 7, 1961\nMr. Harold M. Bixby\n\"Topside\"\nBolton Landing, New Lork\nDear Harold -\nThe Florida Supreme Court seems to be in no hurry to rule\non the Sanibel causeway bond\ncase.\nWill. let you know as soon\nas they rule.\nWhen I last saw you we discussed the possibility of including\na piece of privately owned property in the proposed Sanibel wild-\nlife preserve.\nThis chunk of land contains about 234 acres and it\nSec. 17, I 46 S - R 22 E, and is surrounded by State and\nIt is owned by two separate parties and is listed\nfor sale at $350 per acre with the Sanibel-Captiva Real Estate\nhere.\nI am sending a copy of this letter to the president of the\nFlorida Audubon\nSociety - Mr. John Storer, Under Mountain Road,\nSheffield, Mass.\nI believe the Society has some detailed maps\nthe area we prepared some time ago.\nMr. Storer has been our contact\nwith the I.I.Board in the matter\nof setting aside some 2,000 acres\nof these wet lands for a permanent wildlife preserve.\nPerhaps Mr. Storer has already considered how these\nprivately\nowned lands in Sec. 17 might be included in the preserve.\nbeen most helpful all the way on the proposa: and is experienced in\nsetting up projects of this kind.\nI an asking him to write\nFrom the map it seems you are almost summer neighbors.\nWe are expecting our three grandsons here next week for a visit.\nNever a dull moment then.\nOpal joins me in sending best greetings\nto you and Mrs. Bixby.\nThanks for the good wishes.\nSincerely,\nWieli, Combs\nP.S. The\nSignet\nsay about the\nauthor.\nbook I am sending you portrays more than i can\nMr. and Mrs. Storer are very line people.\n26Bc",
